  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Ymy/DjuPh5Xfn0j2Eq+FP5HCFCk=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:11.917Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "a16z crypto observes stablecoins serving as the settlement layer for agent-to-agent transactions, with a new merchant category emerging: **headless merchants** \u2014 servers with endpoints and per-call pricing, no traditional checkout.\n\n**Data points (late 2025):**\n- x402 processing roughly **$1.6 million per month** in agent-driven payments\n- Stripe's MPP processed **more than 34,000 transactions** in its first week, with fees as low as **$0.003**\n\n**Why it matters:** fee floors of traditional rails (~$0.10+) made per-call pricing impossible; sub-cent fees invert the economics of selling software as granular services.\n\nSource: a16z crypto, \"5 Ways Blockchains Can Help AI Agents\" (https://a16zcrypto.com/posts/article/5-ways-blockchains-help-ai-agents/).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:11.917Z"
    }
  },
